  "spec": {
    "name": "Otto DIY Biped Robot",
    "function": "A small walking robot: two legs with a hip and an ankle SG90 servo each walk, turn and dance, an Arduino Nano runs the gait, and an HC-SR04 ultrasonic sensor in the head sees obstacles so it turns away before it bumps into them, all from four AA batteries.",
    "quote": "I want to build the Otto DIY walking robot: four SG90 servos for hips and ankles, an Arduino Nano, an HC-SR04 as eyes so it walks around obstacles, and four AA batteries. Keep it under 45 euros and 350 grams. Each ankle servo has to lift the whole robot onto one foot with at least 1.5 times the torque, it must not fall over when I nudge it, and it should walk for at least an hour on one set of batteries.",
